===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*terkʷ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|torcion}}, from {{der|en|frm|torsion}}, from {{der|en|LL.|torsiō|torsiōnem}}, from {{der|en|la|tortiō}}, from {{m|la|torqueō||twist, turn}}. See {{m|en|torture}}, {{m|en|-tort}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɔː.ʃən/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-torsion.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtor.ʃɪn/|/ˈtor.ʒɪn/|/ˈtor.ʃən/|/ˈtor.ʒən/|a=GA}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The act of [[turn]]ing or [[twist]]ing, or the state of being twisted; the twisting or [[wrench]]ing of a body by the [[exertion]] of a [[lateral]] [[force]] tending to turn one [[end]] or part of it about a [[longitudinal]] [[axis]], while the other is [[hold|held]] [[fast]] or turned in the opposite direction.
# {{lb|en|math}} A [[finite]] [[order]] element of a [[group]] that, when [[raise]]d to a [[positive]] [[integer]] [[power]] results in the [[identity element]] of the group.
# {{lb|en|math}} An element of a [[homology]] or [[cohomology]] [[group]] for which there exists a non-zero [[integer]] that, when the element is [[multiply|multiplied]] by that integer, yields [[zero]].
# {{lb|en|medicine}} A type of [[holistic]] [[complimentary]] [[medicine]] that involves [[balance|balancing]] [[theoretical]] [[energy]] [[field]]s through [[energy]] [[healing]], [[meditation]], and similar practices.
# {{lb|en|mechanics}} That [[force]] with which a [[thread]], [[wire]], or [[rod]] of any [[material]] [[return]]s, or tends to return, to a state of [[rest]] after it has been [[twist]]ed; [[torsibility]].
# {{lb|en|surgery}} The [[stop]]ping of [[arterial]] [[haemorrhage]] in certain cases, by [[twist]]ing the [[cut]] [[end]] of the [[artery]].

